book: 00.00.10.work

## Goal
Compare Prime work with ordinary file/search/test tools against the same kind of
work with reviewed workshop support modules. Determine whether support reduces
manual operations, errors, correction effort and Director attention. No assumption
that an assisted run must win. Definition lives here; individual investigations and
coordinator returns live in declared N7NN pages.

## Roles and isolation
Director supplies resources and consequential choices. Prime supplies a contextual
Colab question and a fixed benchmark version. A separate Codex bench coordinator
prepares and collects runs and reports the evidence; it does not repair or coach a
run, choose a preferred outcome, or give a tested Prime its hidden assessment key.
Baseline and assisted work run in separate fresh sessions/worker contexts. A single
model solving both sequentially is not a valid clean comparison. Coordinator access
to assessment material is separate from recipient packages.

## First slice
One bounded return-review cycle, not autonomous project execution. Four small case
families: ordinary correction, misleading completion, Director-required design fork,
and genuinely complete work. Matched variants with equivalent decisive evidence.
Both conditions receive equal task/source content and ordinary read/search tools;
only the assisted condition receives the declared reviewed module interfaces.
No arbitrary restriction that makes baseline artificially helpless. Outputs are
review/report and proposed next action, not dispatch or live work-page changes.

## Measurement and interpretation
Fix criteria before answers. Check finding accuracy, appropriate escalation,
preservation of reasons/quotes, unnecessary work, manual tool operations, elapsed
time, usage/caching when exposed, and correction/reviewer effort. Unknown remains
unknown. A private reasoning trace is not required. Rates per model/effort, exact
sources, tool versions, order, prior involvement and deviations are retained.
Matched cases do not guarantee equal difficulty; repeated balanced runs and unseen
cases are needed before claiming general productivity multiples. Subscription usage
percentages are not automatically equivalent to token cost. Failed/abandoned runs
remain in the dataset.

## Build and use
0513.bench-build implements a portable case/collection/assessment harness without
model calls. Preparation snapshots, raw returns and supplied assessments are retained.
Use the N7NN pack/return/notes/review exchange and N1NN custody for the coordinator
handoff. Do not make that readable exchange a second editable copy of a sealed return.
A contextual Colab can challenge this method independently before the first actual
benchmark. The current AR-01 execution hold excludes old inventory/bridge fixtures.
The harness self-tests use new synthetic records and reviewed read-only support.

## Open questions
Actual model/effort choices, spending/run count, supported fresh-session execution
surface and first Director session launch remain explicit choices before model runs.
No universal pass score or model ranking is decided here. Section IDs remain separate.
